  "concept": {
    "movement": "A compact paired hind-foot hop at slow speed, opening into a faster bound. Both feet advance together in matching lanes, the haunches crouch and extend, the hands stay clear of the thighs, and a coherent centered tail balances the body.",
    "attack": "A guarded backward load, one forceful forward hind-foot kick while the other foot stays braced, then a controlled recovery. The long tail counterbalances without claiming weight-bearing support.",
    "death": "A brief forward gathering with the feet planted, followed by a forward chest-and-pelvis collapse. The neck settles with the skull, the released legs and hands relax and the tail follows into a supported still hold."
